ATAM — Risks, Non-Risks, Sensitivity Points, Tradeoffs

Risks:

Ingestion Reliability Risk: Dependence on MQ configurations (DLQ, retry backoff).

Security Risk: Incorrect tenant scoping could cause cross-tenant data leakage.

Cost Risk: Hybrid retrieval increases compute + storage costs.

Performance Risk: Too much metadata filtering slows top-K queries.

Non-Risks:

These areas were tested and confirmed to work as intended:

Autoscaling: HPA responds quickly under load, preventing Core service saturation.

Streaming LLM responses: Tested under 1k concurrent users without degradation.

Circuit-breakers: Proper fallback messaging proven during LMS outage simulation.

Sensitivity Points:

(Small architectural changes cause major system behavior changes.)

Vector DB retrieval latency — sensitive to metadata index structure.

MQ retry settings — small changes can cause backlog buildup.

JWT claim structure — directly tied to secure tenant isolation.

Batch size thresholds — determine GPU/CPU worker throughput.

Tradeoffs:

Performance vs Cost

Hybrid retrieval improves relevance but increases storage + compute cost.

Security vs Modifiability

Tenant-specific RBAC rules add complexity to adapter development.

Availability vs Performance

More aggressive retries improve ingestion reliability but risk message storms.

Simplicity vs Flexibility

Per-tenant namespaces improve isolation but complicate deployments.
